-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  lex_splices_err_stray_between.pcpp - Lexical: a stray backslash between statements

  Break step of lex_splices: a stray backslash between two statements is
  LX0004 and only itself is lost: the statement after it on the same line
  is still read on its own. That statement is 3; on purpose, so its own
  error (SM0613, a statement with no effect) shows it was read. (A stray
  character in the middle of a statement is lex_splices_err_stray: there
  the rest of the statement goes with it.)
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_splices_err_stray_between;

/*
  @@test
    kind error
  @@end
*/

var
  LN: int32;

begin
  LN := 1; \ 3; // ERROR LX0004@12: Invalid character in source // ERROR SM0613@14: statement has no effect
end.
